Template: kodemo/theme
Type: select
Choices: Kodemo Dark, Kodemo Light, Gruvbox Dark, Gruvbox Light, Monokai, Tokyo Night, Kodemo Ocean, AMOLED Black
Default: Kodemo Dark
Description: Color theme for Kodemo:
 Kodemo can start with any of its built-in themes. You can change this at
 any time in File > Settings.

Template: kodemo/rendering
Type: select
Choices: hardware, software
Default: hardware
Description: Rendering method:
 Hardware uses the GPU through OpenGL and is the best choice on almost every
 machine. Software uses Mesa's CPU rasterizer; pick it only if Kodemo fails
 to start or the screen flickers.

Template: kodemo/webkit
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Enable the built-in website preview?
 The live preview uses WebKitGTK. Kodemo can run without it: the editor,
 terminal and AI ghost text keep working.
 .
 If WebKitGTK is already installed, Kodemo uses the system copy. Otherwise
 the installer can install libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0.

Template: kodemo/ai
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Install the local AI ghost-completion model now?
 Qwen 2.5 Coder 0.5B runs entirely on this machine and adds about 400-500 MB
 of disk space. No account, API key or telemetry is involved.
 .
 If you skip it now, Kodemo asks again and downloads the model automatically
 the first time you enable ghost suggestions.

Template: kodemo/model
Type: select
Choices: q4_k_m, q4_0
Default: q4_k_m
Description: Model quality:
 Q4_K_M gives the best suggestions. Q4_0 is smaller and a little faster on
 very old CPUs.
